<title>UK: P&amp;O says Q2 European ferries remain strong.</title>
<headline>P&amp;O says Q2 European ferries remain strong.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-07-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>Peninsular and Oriental Steam Navigation Co said on Tuesday the performance of its European ferries remained strong in the second quarter of 1997 as a result of restricted Eurotunnel SA operations.  </p>
<p>P&amp;O said: &quot;There is continuing pressure on rates but the change between Q1 and Q2 was less pronounced than in previous quarters.&quot;</p>
<p>			P&amp;O CRUISES</p>
<p>				 Capacity Achieved</p>
<p>			     (passenger berth days)</p>
<p>			    2nd Quarter	     Year to date</p>
<p>			  1997	1996	  1997	1996</p>
<p> Princess Cruises  974,458  944,118   1,905,197  1,961,356</p>
<p> P&amp;O Cruises (UK)  356,620  346,170     710,020    698,140</p>
<p>			    Load Factors (pct)</p>
<p>			  2nd Quarter		 Year to date</p>
<p>			1997	1996	    1997	1996</p>
<p> Princess Cruises  99.3	100.0	    99.6     99.8</p>
<p> P&amp;O Cruises (UK)  96.7	95.2	     94.4     94.0</p>
<p>			P&amp;O EUROPEAN FERRIES</p>
<p>			Short Sea Carryings (1)</p>
<p>			  2nd Quarter		 Year to date</p>
<p>			1997	1996	    1997	1996</p>
<p> Passengers     2,703,573 2,522,106     4,452,095 4,097,724</p>
<p> Tourist Vehicles 460,944   407,393	 780,947   700,173</p>
<p> Freight Units    157,814   98,068	  317,633   201,794</p>
<p>Total Carryings UK - Continent (2)</p>
<p>			  2nd Quarter		 Year to date</p>
<p>			1997	1996	    1997	1996</p>
<p> Passengers     3,628,054 3,373,097     5,850,609 5,420,607</p>
<p> Tourist Vehicles 659,085   595,960     1,069,737   973,590</p>
<p> Freight Units    454,846   367,946	 887,204   737,503</p>
<p>P&amp;O said in the first half of 1997 the Short Sea market had grown by over 10 percent year-on-year for tourist vehicle traffic and approximately eight percent for freight traffic.</p>
<p>The P&amp;O Stena Line joint venture on the Short Sea had been cleared by the French government, P&amp;O said. It was expecting announcements by the European Commission and British government soon. --London newsroom +44 171 542 7717</p>
